---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wolverhampton PHV Licensing FAQs — Common Questions Answered"
  description="Clear answers to the most common Wolverhampton private hire licensing questions — renewals, licences, DBS, vehicles and more."
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />

  <main class="md:flex md:justify-center">
    <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-[750px]">
      <h1>Wolverhampton PHV Licensing FAQs</h1>

      <p>
        These are the questions Wolverhampton private hire drivers ask most
        often — renewals, how your licence is issued, DBS, check codes,
        reporting changes, replacements and vehicles — answered in plain
        English. If you're not yet licensed, start with our guides on
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/eligibility/"
          >whether you're eligible for a Wolverhampton PHV licence</a
        >
        and
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/how-to-apply/"
          >how to apply for one</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>Your driver licence</h2>

      <h3>How do I renew my licence?</h3>

      <p>
        You'll need a <strong>Personal Reference Number</strong>, which the
        council sends by email in your renewal letter. If you haven't
        received it and you have less than four weeks left on your licence,
        contact the licensing team directly at
        <a href="mailto:driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk"
          >driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>How will I receive my licence?</h3>

      <p>
        By email. Wolverhampton <strong>no longer issues paper
        licences</strong>. You won't receive a PDF copy of a renewed licence
        until every check on your application is fully complete.
      </p>

      <h3>My operator wants to see a paper licence — what do I do?</h3>

      <p>
        All private hire operators have been told that licences are now
        issued by email. If your licence appears on the council's public
        register, you're allowed to work. Point your operator to the online
        register if they ask for paper.
      </p>

      <h3>How do I know if my licence is valid?</h3>

      <p>
        Check the council's online licence register — your status updates
        there daily. If your current licence is still valid, the register
        shows the original expiry date, even where a renewal has already
        been granted.
      </p>

      <h3>Why didn't I get a full licence term?</h3>

      <p>
        For a <strong>driver licence</strong>, the council emails a letter
        explaining the reason. If you didn't receive it, contact
        <a href="mailto:driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk"
          >driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        For a <strong>vehicle licence</strong>, it's usually the age of the
        vehicle — a vehicle over 10 years old only receives a 6-month
        licence.
      </p>

      <h3>My details aren't showing on the public register</h3>

      <p>
        If you're not on the register, your licence may have expired. If
        you've applied to renew, make sure you've submitted all the mandatory
        documents, or your application will be delayed:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>HMRC Tax Check code</li>
        <li>Medical certificate (including the D4 form)</li>
        <li>Right to Work evidence</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where you can legally drive</h2>

      <p>
        This is one of the most misunderstood areas, so it's worth being
        precise.
      </p>

      <h3>Private hire driver licence</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          You can accept pre-booked journeys anywhere in the country, as long
          as the journey is in a Wolverhampton-licensed private hire vehicle
          and booked through a private hire operator licensed by
          Wolverhampton.
        </li>
        <li>
          You <strong>cannot</strong> ply for hire or use ranks — private
          hire is pre-booked only.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Hackney Carriage (dual) driver licence</h3>

      <ul>
        <li>
          You can ply or stand for hire (use a taxi rank) in a
          Wolverhampton-licensed Hackney Carriage anywhere within
          Wolverhampton.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can also accept pre-booked journeys anywhere in the country.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>DBS and the Update Service</h2>

      <h3>I'm not on the DBS Update Service — what happens?</h3>

      <p>
        If you're not registered on the DBS Update Service, you'll only
        receive a <strong>six-month licence</strong>, and you'll need to
        apply for a new DBS certificate to get your next licence term.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you were on the Update Service and then came off it, you'll need
        to provide a new DBS certificate. The council will email you with
        what is required. There's more detail on DBS and the other entry
        requirements in our
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/eligibility/">eligibility guide</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Check codes and tax</h2>

      <p>
        Every licensed driver and operator must be registered to pay tax and
        prove their right to work. That means two codes:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>HMRC Tax Check code</strong> — a 9-digit code you get from
          gov.uk (search "complete a tax check for a taxi, private hire or
          scrap metal licence"). Required.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Right to Work code</strong> — obtained from gov.uk ("prove
          your right to work"). Required.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        Both codes are submitted through the council's "Provide a Check Code"
        page.
      </p>

      <h2>Reporting changes and issues</h2>

      <h3>How do I report a change of details?</h3>

      <p>
        Use the <strong>MyLicence Portal</strong> (register and log in at
        iApply) to report a change of address, name, contact details, or
        medical circumstances.
      </p>

      <p>
        Hackney Carriage / dual or South Staffordshire licence holders should
        contact the council at
        <a href="mailto:ssdc@wolverhampton.gov.uk">ssdc@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
        > instead.
      </p>

      <h3>
        What if I receive a penalty notice, caution, conviction, reprimand or
        warning?
      </h3>

      <p>
        You <strong>must</strong> report it through the MyLicence Portal.
        Hackney Carriage/dual and South Staffordshire holders report via
        <a href="mailto:ssdc@wolverhampton.gov.uk">ssdc@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h3>I can't access the MyLicence Portal</h3>

      <p>Work through these first:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Confirm you've actually registered.</li>
        <li>
          Check whether you received and accepted your verification code.
        </li>
        <li>Make sure you only signed up once.</li>
        <li>Use the email address on your council record.</li>
        <li>Try clearing your browser cache and cookies.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If it still won't work, try resetting your password and confirm the
        reset email arrives. Passwords must be at least 8 characters with at
        least one uppercase letter, one lowercase letter, one number, and one
        special character from ! @ # $ % ^ &amp; *.
      </p>

      <h2>Replacements and fees</h2>

      <p>
        You'll need proof of ID — either your DVLA driving licence or your
        driver badge.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Replacement badges and lanyards</strong> — contact Driver
          Licensing
          (<a href="mailto:driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk"
            >driver.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
          >)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Replacement pouches and fixing brackets</strong> — contact
          Vehicle Licensing
          (<a href="mailto:vehicle.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk"
            >vehicle.lic@wolverhampton.gov.uk</a
          >)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Item</th>
            <th>Cost</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Driver badge replacement (x2)</td>
            <td>£5</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Lanyard and badge holder</td>
            <td>£1 (£4 if delivered)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Pouch for driver badge</td>
            <td>£1</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Fixing bracket</td>
            <td>£14</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Damaged vehicle plate replacement</td>
            <td>£12</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Training</h2>

      <h3>Why have I been asked to redo the training?</h3>

      <p>
        Any driver who completed Worcestershire County Council's Driver
        Training Programme <strong>before 19 September 2019</strong> is being
        asked to re-attend. The updated course adds new conditions of licence
        and County Lines content.
      </p>

      <p>
        Arrange it directly with Worcestershire County Council
        (<a href="mailto:taxidrivertraining@worcestershire.gov.uk"
          >taxidrivertraining@worcestershire.gov.uk</a
        >). Do it as soon as possible to avoid renewal delays. You'll need to
        provide your name, National Insurance number, driving licence number,
        email, phone number, and licence number.
      </p>

      <h2>Medical certificates</h2>

      <h3>The doctor refused to complete my medical certificate</h3>

      <p>
        You can visit any other GMC-registered medical practitioner to have
        it completed. <strong>Note:</strong> if you are not medically fit to
        drive to Group 2 standard, a driver licence application will be
        refused.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments</h2>

      <h3>My online payment won't go through</h3>

      <p>
        Try a desktop or laptop rather than a mobile device, and use Google
        Chrome rather than your usual browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Applications through third parties</h2>

      <h3>I applied through an operator or third party and can't get an update</h3>

      <p>
        The council has <strong>no approved agents or third parties</strong>.
        Any service a third party provides isn't regulated or controlled by
        the council.
      </p>

      <p>
        The council can only give you information if you have an application
        reference number beginning with <strong>WTP</strong>. If you paid a
        third party to submit your application, you'll need to chase them.
        The council can only assist if you have an email from iApply
        confirming your application was submitted.
      </p>

      <h3>I applied via iApply but got no acknowledgement email</h3>

      <p>
        Check your junk and spam folders. If it's still not there, you
        probably entered an incorrect email address when applying.
      </p>

      <h2>Vehicle questions</h2>

      <p>
        Full vehicle eligibility is covered in our
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/eligibility/">eligibility guide</a>, but
        here are the quick answers that come up most often:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Recording walkaround checks without a smartphone</strong> —
          print and complete the government's driver vehicle condition
          checklist.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Can someone else drive my licensed vehicle?</strong> Yes,
          provided they're insured and hold a relevant Wolverhampton-issued
          driver licence.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Does a brand-new vehicle need an MOT?</strong> Not if it's
          brand new with only delivery mileage (maximum 500 miles).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Personalised number plates</strong> — allowed; see the
          council's "Apply for private registration" page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Surrendering a vehicle licence</strong> — send the licence,
          plate, any stickers and a completed surrender form to City of
          Wolverhampton Council, Chapel Street, Bilston, Wolverhampton WV14
          0PH.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Still have a question?</h2>

      <p>
        For anything not covered here, contact Taxi Licensing and Compliance
        through the council's licensing contact page. This guide summarises
        the council's published FAQs in plain English — always check the
        official council page for the definitive position.
      </p>

      <p>
        Preparing for the knowledge test as well? See our guides on
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/how-to-pass/"
          >how to pass the Wolverhampton PHV test</a
        >
        and
        <a href="/phv-prep-uk/guide/8-key-questions/">the 8 key questions</a>,
        or practise anywhere with the
        <a
          href="https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/phv-prep-uk-taxi-badge-test/id6776364932"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">PHV Prep UK app</a
        >.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>PHV Prep UK is an independent study aid.</strong> It is not
        affiliated with, authorised by, or endorsed by City of Wolverhampton
        Council or any licensing authority. Always refer to the council's
        official website for the definitive licensing position.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
